    ("Text 1: Historian Turner famously formulated the 'Frontier Thesis,' asserting that the continuous availability of free western land shaped American democracy by fostering individualism, egalitarianism, and democratic institutions. \nText 2: Modern revisionist historians argue that Turner’s thesis romanticized settler colonialism while deliberately erasing the catastrophic dispossession, genocide, and displacement experienced by Indigenous nations. \nBased on the texts, what primary criticism would the revisionist historians in Text 2 level against Turner’s model in Text 1?", "It presents a sanitized, celebratory narrative of westward expansion that ignores the violent erasure of Indigenous populations.", "It overestimates the importance of European intellectual traditions in shaping early colonial governance.", "It demonstrates that industrial urbanization was the true primary catalyst of American democratic identity.", "It incorrectly claims that the western frontier was closed prior to the American Civil War.", "雙篇史學批評分析：Turner 的邊疆假說將西部拓荒描繪為孕育民主個人主義的泉源；修正派史學家指責其美化殖民擴張，抹煞了對原住民的種族滅絕與掠奪。修正派的核心批評在於：邊疆學說建構了一種粉飾太平的歌功頌德敘事，遮蔽了對原住民族群的暴力抹除與殘酷掠奪。", "史學批判焦點：指責邊疆學說粉飾暴力拓荒歷史 (sanitized celebratory narrative ignoring erasure of Indigenous populations)。", "批評選項對應 It presents a sanitized, celebratory narrative... ignoring violent erasure of Indigenous...", "revisionist", "/rɪˈvɪʒ.ən.ɪst/", "修正主義的修正派的", "dispossession", "/ˌdɪs.pəˈzeʃ.ən/", "被剝奪財產被驅逐土地剝奪"),
    ("Text 1: Paleontologist Horner proposed that *Tyrannosaurus rex* was primarily an obligate scavenger rather than an active apex predator, pointing to its small eyes, crushing dentition, and large olfactory lobes as adaptations for locating carcasses. \nText 2: Biomechanist Hutchinson demonstrated that bite-mark healing patterns on fossilized herbivorous dinosaurs prove *T. rex* engaged in active predation against living, struggling prey. \nHow does Hutchinson’s evidence (Text 2) challenge Horner’s hypothesis (Text 1)?", "By providing empirical proof of non-fatal predatory attacks on living prey that healed prior to the prey's eventual death.", "By demonstrating that *Tyrannosaurus rex* possessed binocular depth perception superior to modern raptors.", "By proving that scavengers are physiologically incapable of crushing dense mammalian bones.", "By showing that *Tyrannosaurus rex* possessed hollow bones optimized for long-distance marathon pursuit.", "古生物學爭論題：Horner 主張霸王龍是純腐食動物而非主動獵食者；Hutchinson 發現草食恐龍骨骼上的咬痕出現了癒合骨痂，證實霸王龍曾襲擊活生生會掙扎反抗的獵物。該證據如何挑戰 Horner：提供了霸王龍主動襲擊活體獵物、且傷口在獵物最終死亡前曾癒合的實質物證！", "挑戰論據：咬痕癒合證實襲擊時為活體 (empirical proof of non-fatal attacks that healed)。", "挑戰選項對應 By providing empirical proof of non-fatal predatory attacks on living prey that healed...", "scavenger", "/ˈskæv.ɪn.dʒɚ/", "食腐動物撿拾腐肉者", "olfactory", "/ɑːlˈfæk.tɚ.i/", "嗅覺的嗅覺器官的")
